sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/cli/instance/rename.mdx, ADR 0244, R1 record-only; read-only rule (Nick 2026-11-02): the Gateway checks the Node agent's checkout facts, like instance:register.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 5 (its own example: rename records the branch the Node agent reported, with no run).
  %% Decided: Nick 2026-11-02, this chart is the ideal record-only flow. Implemented in the observer pass (agent 0.7.0, 2026-11-03).
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: instance:rename
  %% kind: instance.rename
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  loop continuously, on change
    Note over A: Observe checkouts<br/>under the apps root
    %%> What it observes:
    %%> - each Git checkout under `<apps-root>/<project-slug>/<name>`, Instance 42's included
    %%> - its top level, origin, symbolic `HEAD` and commit
    %%> How:
    %%> - event-driven, with inotify or FSEvents, on `.git/HEAD`, `refs/heads`, `packed-refs`, `config` and each worktree `HEAD`
    %%> - a full resync every 10 minutes and at agent start
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - read-only; the Node agent never changes a Node
    A->>GW: Report observations<br/>with observed_at
    %%> What it sends:
    %%> - what changed since the last report, with the time it was observed
    Note over GW: Store latest facts<br/>per Node, per checkout
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway always has a recent picture of the checkouts on each app-dev Node
  end
  CLI->>GW: instance:rename 42
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:rename 42 --branch=t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> - syntax: `instance:rename <instance> --branch=BRANCH [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - a local branch you already checked out, for example after `git branch -m t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - it does not rename the Instance, move its directory or change Git `HEAD`
  %%> - `--domain` returns `operation.kind_unavailable`
  Note over CLI: Require a rename field
  %%> Result:
  %%> - with neither `--branch` nor `--domain`, returns `validation.failed`; no request is sent
  opt --domain
    GW--xCLI: Domain rename unavailable<br/>operation.kind_unavailable
    %%> Result:
    %%> - refuses before changing any field, also when `--branch` is supplied
  end
  opt --branch
    Note over GW: Check against the facts<br/>HEAD · identity · observed_at
    %%> Requirements:
    %%> - Instance 42 is an active development checkout or linked worktree on Node 12
    %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
    %%> - the branch is a valid local branch name
    %%> Checks in the agent's latest report:
    %%> - symbolic `HEAD` of Instance 42's checkout names `t3code/login-redirect`
    %%> - the checkout still matches its recorded top level and origin
    %%> - the report is fresh enough to trust
    %%> Not needed:
    %%> - no Swamp run and no SSH: the fact is already recorded (R1)
    alt HEAD names the branch
      Note over GW: Record the branch<br/>selected_branch · override
      %%> Result:
      %%> - `selected_branch` and `branch_override` of Instance 42 become `t3code/login-redirect`
      %%> - recording the already recorded branch keeps its existing override
      %%> - a dirty or unpublished branch can be recorded
      GW-->>CLI: Branch recorded<br/>Instance 42 · t3code/login-red…
      %%> What you get:
      %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
    else other branch, detached or stale
      GW--xCLI: Refused or can't verify<br/>instance.branch_not_checked_out
      %%> When:
      %%> - symbolic `HEAD` names another branch or is detached
      %%> - or the checkout no longer matches its recorded identity
      %%> - or the latest report is too old: the refusal says it can't verify
      %%> Result:
      %%> - Instance 42 keeps its recorded branch; nothing is recorded
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - check out the branch, wait for the next agent report, then run `instance:rename` again
    end
  end
